# .gitattributes — Gate 25
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. The repo carried a mixed LF/CRLF state and `core.autocrlf`
# is `true` both locally and globally, so line endings are rewritten on
# checkout and any RECORDED line-ending state goes stale the moment someone
# clones. `text=auto` moves that decision from a per-machine git config into
# the repo, where it is reviewable.
#
# THIS FILE WAS MEASURED BEFORE IT WAS WRITTEN, not reasoned about.
# `git ls-files --eol` reported the index as 80 `i/lf`, 95 `i/-text` and 3
# `i/none` — and, decisively, **ZERO files stored with CRLF in the index**.
# So `text=auto` renormalises nothing: it codifies the state the repo is
# already in rather than changing it. That is the entire reason it was safe to
# declare broadly.
#
# `git add --renormalize` WAS DELIBERATELY NOT RUN. Adding this file changes
# how git treats FUTURE checkouts; renormalising rewrites the working tree NOW.
# Doing both at once would put a whole-tree line-ending rewrite in the same
# commit as ordinary code changes, where no reviewer could separate them.

* text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- binaries
#
# THE 95 BINARIES ARE DECLARED EXPLICITLY, AND THIS IS THE LOAD-BEARING HALF
# OF THE FILE. 93 of them are PNGs and 92 of those are the visual regression
# baselines — the entire net this project's correctness rests on. A `text`
# rule that ever caught them would rewrite bytes inside a compressed stream
# and corrupt every one, silently, on the next checkout.
#
# Git already infers all 95 correctly (`i/-text` above), so these lines change
# nothing today. They exist so that a future broadening of the `text` rule
# cannot reach them by accident. `binary` is the built-in macro for
# `-diff -merge -text`.
#
# Census at Gate 25 — the only binary extensions tracked in this repo:
#   *.png   93   (92 e2e baselines + public/media/academy/monarchacademy_img.png)
#   *.webp   2   (public/media)
# `*.svg` (4 files) is deliberately NOT here: SVG is XML, i.e. genuinely text,
# and forcing `binary` on it would lose diffs for no benefit. It is left to
# `text=auto`.

*.png  binary
*.webp binary
